<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Kosovo: Protests and outrage after a woman was killed despite repeatedly seeking assistance from the authorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44a451e4ad3ee2c87ac6b9df837a73afb3a6d226c80050c568627399e43709e4</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-protests-and-outrage-after-a-woman-was-killed-despite-repeatedly-seeking-assistance-from-the-/a-79856726--c1f512250aa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-protests-and-outrage-after-a-woman-was-killed-despite-repeatedly-seeking-assistance-from-the-authorities/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for Palestine: Karate's Mariam Bsharat a rare sporting success</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8bff90f9ee9c4f849f9f1f6ddfc4fc0ea6e930442c964658ca218a637f3b63</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-palestine-karate-s-mariam-bsharat-a-rare-sporting-success/a-79851806--7ec89a6ed055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-palestine-karate-s-mariam-bsharat-a-rare-sporting-success/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's shifting role in the global drug trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f402d157499114f816dee9cb1d9902fdb9e025ce36e623e62de7e6081633226</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720--a33472b9e48a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent discoveries of meth labs suggest parts of Africa are moving beyond drug transit and becoming sites of synthetic drug production.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Potter films turns 25 ahead of new TV series' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d08cf29079fc5cd472ce6b89230e73f1450e0c4131caa9304c5fc99eb6b36a67</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130--db1dcb8d550c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2001, "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone" hit cinemas and took the world by storm. Today, anticipation for the new series is high, but its creator, J.K. Rowling, remains a controversial figure.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ad511d9f5729eecd60729bb162daba672fd467ae25acec617ee982529b53c5b</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU says Montenegro on track to become bloc's next member state by 2028</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70965ce87333445845a846d9520f576acf0bb8091bfa994a8aa247b828886ef</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:26:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011--2c07b9ca6077.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brussels says Montenegro is likely to become the EU's 28th member state, followed by Albania and Moldova. It said Ukraine needed to speed up reforms and offered fresh hope to Serbia following elections last month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:672eeba8d5de5a10ef28cd4fb22320790f37eb07bb124699f1f51b673da81859</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Commerce chief calls for stable US trade relations after midterms, warning that uncertainty over Trump's tariff policies remains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5e9d31121c78b6a3a7ac42231fcb36f283382bc17ab2e54366ca166337c5d2</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-calls-for-stable-us-trade-relations-after-midterms-warning-that-uncertai/live-79854127--f5c0714a5ea7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-calls-for-stable-us-trade-relations-after-midterms-warning-that-uncertainty-over-trump-s-tariff-policies-remains/live-79854127?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German business is pinning its hopes on greater stability in US trade relations after a midterm blow for Donald Trump. Meanwhile, Germany's automakers appear to be feeling less gloomy than in recent years. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbc14b466aa4fb2e636a507e1ad5edc01ce0b5b1a13d3195e9efaa0910f1fec8</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Democrats win House and Senate from Republicans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3228e31850da41742b7410b9d98df69d1a378bc8b79f03649e997d68a97a272</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-win-house-and-senate-from-republicans/live-79829440--9b6818e1e585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-win-house-and-senate-from-republicans/live-79829440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Democratic Party gained control of the House and Senate, delivering a stinging rebuke to US President Donald Trump and his Republican Party. Follow DW's live updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary opens communist-era secret police files identifying informants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac2972c1be843fdd3dbd466f8eb55036a8a63ac9ab73fd19797f9d13415e7ab</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-police-files-identifying-informants/a-79853492--bea146ac21f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-police-files-identifying-informants/a-79853492?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The archives name thousands of former informants who spied on citizens for the state security services during decades of one-party rule. The prime minister said "many families will now face difficult information."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wawira Njirum, Kenya's school feeder and German Africa Prize recipient</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a7b101d765b19995bf59e715e4c760213afdf6744cde99bcf0dab229726c01a</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wawira-njirum-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537--3b2d259b9566.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wawira-njirum-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a small fundraiser to a major enterprise, Wawira Njiru's Kenyan school feeding scheme has been more successful than she ever thought possible. She's now being awarded the German Africa Prize.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>BMW reports lower Q3 earnings as China woes mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f44cec7cd7c33f91a885f5247debbc52f26e8bf3d91e847bf2457215ddd67c25</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b08bed1ab0d0173deaca26ac74a7fbb98c014bb13957c239abbc8383ee4d182</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Africans vote in local elections in test for ANC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6cee8ceb8150f0275364c920c62f74814edcaad9f7d6e8a479195d3ee7ada5b5</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-local-elections-in-test-for-anc/a-79851651--51661e07c56a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-local-elections-in-test-for-anc/a-79851651?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Failing public services, corruption and high crime rates have led to growing frustration among South African voters. That could lead to further losses for the ANC.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What US midterm elections mean for Ukraine, Iran and elsewhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:247c4de981635a1670ef930de1ce82321eb20ff65ae755935f2bc849c1132b7a</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423--c94a74658887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans will no longer control the US Congress after the Democrats flipped both chambers in the midterm elections. The outcome could impact conflicts in Europe and the Middle East.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US midterm election results: Democrats flip House and Senate. Here's what else the data tell us</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f24f9d65114562a163eadb3ab28c45dc387f346fd2dd9c1cfc239d59b38cf5cb</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:27:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T06:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterm-election-results-democrats-flip-house-and-senate-here-s-what-else-the-data-tell-us/a-79841886--a2c25e2ff247.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterm-election-results-democrats-flip-house-and-senate-here-s-what-else-the-data-tell-us/a-79841886?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though vote counts are still ongoing, Democrats have won clear majorities in both the US House and Senate. DW takes a look at who voted Republican, who voted Democrat, and what it all means.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Election body opens door for voter reinclusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d8cd077bb3f3bc7b19894b62dee88039176407635a6626d822db6b3997f9fb</id><updated>2026-11-04T16:25:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-election-body-opens-door-for-voter-reinclusion/live-79849888--daa3a076e9e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-election-body-opens-door-for-voter-reinclusion/live-79849888?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian poll body said no action will be taken against deleted voters for using Form 6 for re-enrolment in voter rolls. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1aa0cf084